=======================================================================
 test_poisson_3d_refine_letters - 3D Poisson disk demo: the word LaGriT
=======================================================================

WHAT THIS IS

  A 3D demo of the Poisson disk sampler with a variable resolution
  field:

      createpts / poisson_disk / 3d_box / mo_box_poi / H_REFINE_SIZE / &
           connect / letters_h_field.mlgi

  The box [-4, 50] x [-4, 14] x [-2, 2] is filled with tets whose size
  h grows with distance from a line drawing of the word "LaGriT":
  h = 0.16 at the letters, rising with slope 0.35 to 1.0 about 2.9
  units away. The deck first turns the line drawing into a dense set of
  vertices (extrude to a thin quad strip, split to triangles, refine
  to edges <= 0.2), because compute/distance_field measures the
  distance to VERTICES only.

  It is the user's demo deck 3D_LaGriT_poi.lgi (Feb 19 2026), renamed
  and run at HALF THE ORIGINAL RESOLUTION for speed (see RUN TIME).
  The checker and picture code are shared with ../test_poisson_3d.

QUICK START

  ./run_poisson_3d_letters.sh  [path-to-lagrit]

  Default: build/lagrit of this checkout. Or give a path or a program on PATH; the
  runner is sh, which cannot see a bash alias or function.

  then open, in a web browser,

      logs/summary.html

  To re-check outputs already in this directory without running LaGriT:

  ./run_poisson_3d_letters.sh --check-only

  Requires: LaGriT, Python 3 (standard library only), a POSIX shell.

