-----------------------------------------------------------------------
RUN TIME
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

  The original deck (h 0.08) took about 66 minutes on the user's Mac
  with the OLD build (LaGriT 3.3.4, Dec 2025): the h field dump is
  stamped 15:13 and the mesh 16:19, so nearly all of it went into
  sampling ~49 000 vertices. (The 3D suite samples 117 000 in 44 s.)
  First real run at h 0.16 on the refactored build (Oct 10 2026):
  LaGriT 177 s. The build AND h both changed, so the two cannot yet
  be separated.

  The h field lookup grid now dominates the file sizes: the driver
  sizes it 1.5 x ceiling(L/h) per axis over the box grown by h, so at
  h 0.16 it is 510 x 172 x 40 = 3 508 800 points (spacing 0.107 =
  0.67 h). The old build used 270 x 90 x 20 at h 0.08 (spacing 0.20 =
  2.5 h). out_letters_h_field.inp is therefore several hundred MB.

  The whole suite took 151 s on Oct 10 2026 without the field dump
  (225 s with it). The checks take about 15 s (case 10 s, picture 4 s). With the field
  dump uncommented, add its write time in LaGriT and 29 s to check it.

  RELEASE BUILD (Oct 11 2026): the build above had no C++ or Fortran
  optimisation (CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE empty). Rebuilt with
  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release: this suite 155 s -> 38 s; time_letters.sh
  gives prep 1 s, h field 2 s, sampling 17 s (was 131 s), connect and
  output 2 s. Build Release (lagclean does).

  WHERE THE TIME GOES: timing/time_letters.sh [lagrit] runs the deck
  in four stages (prep; + h field; + sampling; + connect) and prints
  the cost of each. Not a test; nothing is judged. Takes about 3 times
  as long as the suite.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
RESULTS
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

  Rows: run, deck, case_01, field.

  PASS   every HARD check holds
  SKIP   field row only: no field dump (the default, see FILES)
  FAIL   anything else. The exit status is nonzero on any FAIL.

  HARD checks (exact definitions in check_test_poisson_3d.py):

  run     lagrit exit status 0; one createpts echo and one
          "poisson_disk_3d exit" line; no POISSON DISK error or warning
          block on stdout
  deck    the .cases line matches the defines in effect at the
          createpts line, its .mlgi, and the file the field's source
          mesh object is dumped to
  case    mesh written, tets only, every vertex in the box, no
          duplicate vertex, no inverted or zero-volume tet, no unused
          vertex, no triangle in more than 2 tets, e_vol > 0
  field   only if the dump line is uncommented: h_field_att =
          min(1.0, max(0.16, 0.35 dfield)) at every point, and equal
          to the checker's own distance-based h at a sample of 20 000
          points (relative error < 1e-8)

  MEASURED, NOT JUDGED (in the case block of the summary page):
  spacing d / max(h_p, h_q) by pair class, nearest-neighbour d / h,
  tracking of h by band, wall gap, hull faces off the box, missing
  volume, radius ratio, dihedral angles, and LaGriT's own e_vol /
  edgemin / edgemax ranges.

  Two runner warnings in lagrit.out are LaGriT's own and expected:
  grid2grid (hextotet) on the flat extruded strip reports "Volumes le
  zero not removed" and "Duplicate points not removed". They are
  listed, not judged.

  Baseline: the user's original run (h 0.08, old build), measured
  with this checker:
    48 958 vertices, 306 701 tets, every HARD check met;
    interior pairs down to 0.42 h (11 276 below 0.9 h), most just below
    the letters' top bars; nearest-neighbour d/h median 1.05;
    smallest dihedral 0.084 deg, 1 302 tets under 5 deg;
    6 interior vertices within 0.003 of a box face, so 34 hull faces
    lie off the box (3.6e-6 of the volume missing).
  These are for the quality round; nothing here judges them yet.

  First real run, h 0.16, refactored build (Oct 10 2026), all PASS:
    24 830 vertices, 150 603 tets, LaGriT 177 s;
    hull = the box exactly (0 faces off it), closest interior vertex
    0.86 h from a face;
    interior pairs down to 0.77 h (53 below 0.9 h); nearest-neighbour
    d/h p05 0.98, median 1.06; tracking spread 1.04;
    face-face pairs down to 0.80 h (167 below 0.9 h);
    smallest dihedral 0.27 deg, 395 tets under 5 deg (0.26 %).

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
READING THE PICTURE
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

  TOP OF THE PAGE: the mesh cut normal to z at z = 0.05 (mid-thickness
  of the letter strip), seen from +z, as in ParaView: every tet whose
  centroid has z > 0.05 is removed, so the cut is made of whole tets.
  Each tet is coloured by edgemax (its longest edge, from
  quality/edge_max/y), blue = short, red = long; shading by facet
  direction shows the jagged cut. The letters should stand out in
  blue with a smooth blue-to-red grading away from them.

  CASE PICTURE (below the case block):
  TOP         top view: vertices in a slab |z| < h through the letters.
              Blue = interior vertex, grey = on a box face.
  SIDE        side view, slab through y = 5.
  MIDDLE L    nearest-neighbour spacing / h (should peak just above 1).
  MIDDLE R    smallest dihedral angle per tet; dashed lines 5 and 10 deg.
  BOTTOM L    each interior vertex's nearest-neighbour distance against
              its distance to the letters, with h(d) in red. Good
              tracking = dots just above the red line.
  BOTTOM R    box-face vertices: spacing / h of the field there.

